==========================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
==========================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - H1 next-year ΔGM (headline): β=-0.0152**, p=0.013 (-0.24pp per 1-SD)
      => SUPPORTED; stable across ladder. Leans post-COVID & non-US (see T12/T13).
  - H2 same-year ΔCFO: β=-0.1161***, p=0.000 (-1.87pp per 1-SD); CONTEMPORANEOUS (year t, not t+1).
      => Strongest & most universal ASSOCIATION, but same-year -> it is a concurrent cash-drain signal, NOT an early-warning forecast. Only H1/H3/H4 are forward-looking (t+1).
  - H3 returns (peer EW): Q5−Q1=-0.0474 (t=-3.03)
      => SUPPORTED equal-weighted; value-weighted insignificant -> effect in smaller firms.
  - H4 distress: χ²=8.04, p=0.005 (17% vs 13%)
      => SUPPORTED full-panel & US-only; NOT significant ex-US (χ²=0.56) — likely power (113 firms).
  - Placebo battery (T14): Prior-growth p=0.14; permuted p=0.53 (both null)
      => Real effect is not a spurious artifact; reverse-causality and shuffle both null.
  - US vs international (T13): H1 weak US-only (p~0.19) but stronger ex-US (p=0.01); H2 holds in both; H4 holds full-panel & US-only but NOT ex-US (chi2=0.56).
      => Disclose: H2 is the only universally-robust result. H1 carried by non-US firms; H4 carried by US firms; H3 equal-weighted. Panel is 59% US.
  - Subperiod (T12): H1 not significant pre-COVID; significant post-COVID. H2 both.
      => H1 leans on post-2020 inventory-glut era — disclose.
  - Sector concentration: Demoted to Phase 6 robustness; rejected there.
      => Not a core hypothesis here (see outline 4A).
  - Independence of evidence (CRITICAL): GM_distress = 1[ΔGM < -2pp]: H4 is a binary recoding of H1 outcome (~91% identical).
      => H1 and H4 are TWO LENSES on ONE margin relationship, not independent pillars. Distinct channels: MARGIN (H1/H4), CASH (H2), RETURNS (H3) = 3, not 4.
  - Multiple testing: H1 p=0.014 fails strict Bonferroni (0.0125 at 4 tests); H2/H3/H4 pass.
      => Report H1 as significant at 0.05 but marginal under multiplicity correction.

